WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:24.372
On Saturday morning Riley put her Supertrek on the bike rack and climbed into the car with the rest of her family.

2
00:00:24.373 --> 00:00:31.187
"Ready, Riley?" Mr. Clark asked as they drove toward the tryout trail.

3
00:00:31.188 --> 00:00:34.625
"As ready as I'll ever be," Riley murmured.

4
00:00:34.627 --> 00:00:39.529
"She's ready," Jordan said. "I have confidence in her."

5
00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.272
"Me too," Mrs. Clark said.

6
00:00:42.273 --> 00:00:49.880
"Hey, what's going on?" Riley said as they pulled into the parking lot at the field.

7
00:00:49.881 --> 00:00:54.861
Two police cars sat side by side, their lights flashing.

8
00:00:54.862 --> 00:01:06.009
"Oh no . . . ," Jordan murmured. The Blue Demons' new trail was filled with deep holes and tire tracks from several large vehicles.

9
00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:10.926
"Maybe vandals drove all over the soft dirt," Mr. Clark said.

10
00:01:10.927 --> 00:01:17.505
Riley nodded. The jumps were gone, and trash was strewn all around the track.

11
00:01:17.506 --> 00:01:25.381
Coach Adams and two other men were talking to the police officers as riders looked on, disbelief and anger on their faces.

12
00:01:25.382 --> 00:01:28.071
Riley and Jordan joined the group.

13
00:01:28.072 --> 00:01:36.581
"The track is toast," Delaney said when he saw them. "Some jerks in four-wheel trucks thought it would be fun to trash our track."

14
00:01:36.582 --> 00:01:45.415
Sofia's eyes burned with anger. "We spent a year raising money to build this track. Then in one night, somebody ruined it!"

15
00:01:45.416 --> 00:01:49.984
"Do the police know who did this?" Jordan asked.

16
00:01:49.985 --> 00:01:58.222
"Mr. Ravi, the guy who sold us the land, saw a bunch of guys driving trucks past his farm last night," Delaney replied.

17
00:01:58.223 --> 00:02:02.299
"But it was late. He didn't get a good look at the drivers."

18
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:07.902
Coach Adams called for everyone to gather around.

19
00:02:07.903 --> 00:02:12.293
"First, thank you for coming today," he began.

20
00:02:12.294 --> 00:02:19.126
"As you can see, we've got a problem. Last night vandals damaged our track, and it's not usable today.

21
00:02:19.127 --> 00:02:22.948
The police assure me they'll find out who did this."

22
00:02:22.949 --> 00:02:30.527
He glanced over the crowd of eager riders. "Racing season starts soon so we need to hold our tryout quickly.

23
00:02:30.528 --> 00:02:34.683
Luckily, the racing community has stepped up to help."

24
00:02:34.684 --> 00:02:44.772
He motioned for the second man to step forward. "This is Coach Hopewell, the head coach of the Racing Raptors."

25
00:02:44.773 --> 00:02:47.820
Everyone looked at each other in surprise.

26
00:02:47.821 --> 00:02:54.028
The Racing Raptors were the Blue Demons' biggest rivals. What was the coach doing here?

27
00:02:54.029 --> 00:02:59.755
"Coach Hopewell has offered to let us use their track instead," Coach Adams went on.

28
00:02:59.756 --> 00:03:10.250
Riley gasped and clapped a hand to her mouth. The Racing Raptors' track was on Hawk Mountain—where Jordan had her accident!

29
00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:14.073
"This feels like a bad omen," Riley thought.

30
00:03:14.074 --> 00:03:24.155
The crowd broke up, and everyone headed to their cars for the thirty-minute drive up Hawk Mountain to the Racing Raptors' track.

31
00:03:24.156 --> 00:03:29.501
Riley was quiet as her family pulled out of the parking lot.

32
00:03:29.502 --> 00:03:37.653
"You'll be fine," Jordan said quickly. "The Racing Raptors' track is almost exactly like the Demons' practice track."

33
00:03:37.654 --> 00:03:47.067
Riley shook her head. "I didn't get to test much of the practice track, remember? I crashed. Plus, the Racing Raptors' track is where—"

34
00:03:47.068 --> 00:03:54.632
"Never mind," Jordan cut her off. "Stop thinking about that, and focus on your ride."

35
00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:59.955
Riley nodded and then turned to stare out the car window.

36
00:03:59.956 --> 00:04:07.550
At the Racing Raptors' track, Mrs. Clark went with Riley to the sign-up table.

37
00:04:07.551 --> 00:04:14.867
Mrs. Clark signed the waivers, and Riley showed her USA Cycling membership card without saying a word.

38
00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:19.102
Sofia handed her a race number. "Good luck, Riley."

39
00:04:19.103 --> 00:04:21.025
"Thanks."

40
00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:28.034
Riley and her mother headed to where Mr. Clark had set up chairs to watch the race.

41
00:04:28.035 --> 00:04:34.937
Riley handed Jordan her number, and Jordan carefully pinned it onto Riley's jersey.

42
00:04:34.938 --> 00:04:39.600
"Sixteen is my lucky number," Jordan said with a smile.

43
00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:43.597
"And it brought you terrible luck!" Riley burst out.

44
00:04:43.598 --> 00:04:53.170
"Riley, listen to me. You're going to have a great ride. And you're not me. In fact, you're a better rider than I am.

45
00:04:53.171 --> 00:04:58.653
You've got a lot more determination than I do. I've always been jealous of that."

46
00:04:58.654 --> 00:05:02.833
"Really?" Riley stared at her sister, surprised.

47
00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:10.244
"I might be the speed queen, but focus and determination are the things that win the race," Jordan said firmly.

48
00:05:10.245 --> 00:05:14.149
"Wherever the brain goes, the body follows."

49
00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:22.644
Riley threw her arms around her sister in a strong hug, afraid if she said anything, she'd burst into tears.

50
00:05:22.645 --> 00:05:26.651
Jordan hugged her back. "Good luck."

51
00:05:26.652 --> 00:05:33.212
Riley nodded. "Thanks." Then she suddenly spotted Quinn among a group of riders.

52
00:05:33.213 --> 00:05:39.878
Her fancy bike shone like it had just come out of the store, and several people stood admiring it.

53
00:05:39.879 --> 00:05:43.021
"Maybe I'll wish her luck," Riley thought.

54
00:05:43.022 --> 00:05:50.873
Quinn was annoying, but good sportsmanship was important. Especially if they were going to be on the same team after today.

55
00:05:50.874 --> 00:05:55.218
Riley approached the other girl.

56
00:05:55.219 --> 00:05:58.047
"Hey," Quinn said coldly.

57
00:05:58.048 --> 00:06:06.112
"Look, I'm sorry about what happened in the gym," Riley began. "I didn't mean to sound like a know-it-all."

58
00:06:06.113 --> 00:06:10.117
"Whatever." Quinn looked down at her feet.

59
00:06:10.118 --> 00:06:19.919
"Well, good luck with your ride," Riley said. "And trust me, I'm really not trying to sabotage you." She smiled.

60
00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:26.658
"When I make the team, I'll need a good teammate like you." She turned to go.

61
00:06:26.659 --> 00:06:30.932
"What do you think of this trail?" Quinn asked abruptly.

62
00:06:30.933 --> 00:06:40.593
Riley halted. "Everyone says it's a lot like the Demons' practice trail. But it's longer and has a couple of extra jumps.

63
00:06:40.594 --> 00:06:43.561
One of the jumps is pretty tough."

64
00:06:43.562 --> 00:06:47.640
"Have you ever made it?" Quinn asked, eyeing the track.

65
00:06:47.641 --> 00:06:55.728
"Nope," Riley replied. "It's my first ride here. But this is the trail where Jordan had her accident."

66
00:06:55.729 --> 00:07:02.957
"Oh!" Quinn exclaimed. She looked closely at Riley, and Riley suddenly flushed.

67
00:07:02.958 --> 00:07:08.305
Why had she just blurted that out—to Quinn, of all people?

68
00:07:08.306 --> 00:07:19.221
Riley waved before Quinn could say anything more. "See you later." Then she hurried back to her family to wait for the tryout to start.

69
00:07:19.222 --> 00:07:24.949
A few minutes later Coach Adams lifted a megaphone.

70
00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:30.622
"Good morning, riders. I truly appreciate your patience with our last-minute location change.

71
00:07:30.623 --> 00:07:34.373
It's finally time to get this event started."

72
00:07:34.374 --> 00:07:39.124
"Woo-hoo!" Riders cheered loudly.

73
00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:46.330
"As you know," the coach went on, "today's race is for riders to qualify for the Blue Demons team.

74
00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:50.763
The two riders in each age group with the best times will make the team.

75
00:07:50.764 --> 00:07:56.355
We'll start with the junior division, ages 9 to 12. Good luck, everyone!"

76
00:07:56.356 --> 00:08:02.043
The riders lined up according to their age and gender.

77
00:08:02.045 --> 00:08:10.586
Riley and Quinn were the oldest to try out in the girls' junior division, so they were at the rear of the line.

78
00:08:10.587 --> 00:08:18.506
Riley looked over the younger riders. One or two girls were fast riders, but they were probably nothing to worry about.

79
00:08:18.507 --> 00:08:24.076
Even if Quinn posted the fastest time, Riley could still win a spot on the team.

80
00:08:24.077 --> 00:08:34.985
She swallowed hard. If she didn't get spooked by those jumps.
